@namespace NSail.Components
@typeparam TValue
@inherits NsFieldBase<TValue>

@* The refusal line alone: a field with no input, no label and no outline, for a member a
   composed editor edits without rendering a field for it (an attendee list, drawn as a panel of
   rows). Being RENDERED is what anchors an issue — NsForm draws under a member only when a
   field announced that identifier — so this is what an editor places to be announced, and
   NsFieldBase does the announcing and the reading off the EditContext exactly as it does for a
   field that has a box.

   The expression belongs to the PAGE, not to the editor: FieldIdentifier resolves the owner
   object the member hangs off, so a For written inside an editor would name the editor and
   never match the model the form holds.

   Clean, it renders nothing at all — the member it answers for costs the surface no height
   until something refuses it. *@
<NsFieldHelper Text="@Helper" Message="@GetErrorText()" Shown />

@code {

    // The anchor holds no value — nothing binds through it — so Required has nothing of its own
    // to judge and must not be allowed to mint a refusal from the base's client-side check: the
    // unset Value reads as empty, and "Problems.Required" posted here is a refusal nobody can
    // clear, because there is no box to fill. A requirement over a composed editor's member is
    // the server's, drawn here when it answers.
    protected override bool IsValueEmpty()
    {
        return false;
    }
}
